## Mod Development Guidelines

### Fabric Mod Structure
- Main class: `BasicStorage.java` implements `ModInitializer`
- Client class: `BasicStorageClient.java` for client-side code
- Register components in `onInitialize()` method
- Use proper Fabric API patterns

### Block Registration
- Register in `BlockRegistry.init()`
- Crate blocks extend `CrateBlock` class
- Crate station blocks extend `CrateStationBlock` class
- Use proper block properties and settings

### Item Registration
- Register in `ItemRegistry.init()`
- Crate hammer is a custom item
- Items can have custom behaviors via mixins

### Data Component System
- Register components in `DataComponentRegistry.init()`
- Use `CrateSlotComponent` for crate item storage
- Access via `ItemStack.get(ComponentType)`

### Testing Requirements
- Test crate creation and item storage
- Verify item storage and retrieval works correctly
- Test crate station GUI functionality
- Verify data component persistence
- Test crate hammer functionality
- Ensure compatibility with other mods

### Version Compatibility
- Target Minecraft 1.21
- Use Fabric Loader 0.16.9+
- Require Fabric API 0.102.0+1.21
- Requires Java 21
